// The surface names `markup`, and the module beside it exports `markupCents`.
// One typo, and the two halves of it are the same fact: the re-export does not
// resolve, and the name it meant to reach is reached by nothing. Only the
// first is reported. `dead-code` reads this file to decide what reaches what,
// so a line of it that did not resolve is a line the rule cannot count on —
// and the fix for the typo is the fix for both.
from "//lib/money/cents" export { markup };
